# Data Access Patterns

## Query helpers live in `src/db/queries/`

All direct Drizzle calls must be encapsulated in helper functions inside `src/db/queries/`. Server Components and Server Actions must never call `db.*` directly — they always go through these helpers.

File layout:
```
src/db/queries/
  decks.ts   ← deck reads & writes
  cards.ts   ← card reads & writes
  index.ts   ← re-exports everything
```

Each helper receives `userId` as an explicit parameter (ownership is always enforced inside the helper, never left to the caller).

```typescript
// src/db/queries/decks.ts
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decksTable, InsertDeck, SelectDeck } from "@/schema";
import { and, eq } from "drizzle-orm";

export async function getDecksByUser(userId: string): Promise<SelectDeck[]> {
  return db.select().from(decksTable).where(eq(decksTable.userId, userId));
}

export async function getDeckById(
  deckId: string,
  userId: string
): Promise<SelectDeck | undefined> {
  const [deck] = await db
    .select()
    .from(decksTable)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));
  return deck;
}

export async function insertDeck(
  values: Omit<InsertDeck, "id" | "createdAt">
): Promise<void> {
  await db.insert(decksTable).values(values);
}

export async function updateDeck(
  deckId: string,
  userId: string,
  patch: Partial<Pick<InsertDeck, "title" | "description">>
): Promise<void> {
  await db
    .update(decksTable)
    .set(patch)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));
}

export async function deleteDeck(deckId: string, userId: string): Promise<void> {
  await db
    .delete(decksTable)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));
}
```

## Reads: Server Components → query helpers

Server Components resolve the user with `auth()`, then call query helpers. Never call `db.*` inline.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — raw Drizzle in a server component
export default async function DecksPage() {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  const decks = await db.select().from(decksTable).where(eq(decksTable.userId, userId));
  return <DeckList decks={decks} />;
}

// ❌ BAD — fetching in a client component
"use client";
useEffect(() => {
  fetch("/api/decks").then(...);
}, []);

// ✅ GOOD — server component delegates to a query helper
import { getDecksByUser } from "@/db/queries";

export default async function DecksPage() {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) redirect("/sign-in");

  const decks = await getDecksByUser(userId);
  return <DeckList decks={decks} />;
}
```

## Mutations: Server Actions → query helpers

Server Actions validate input with Zod, then delegate to query helpers. Never call `db.*` inline.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — mutation in a route handler
export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const body = await req.json();
  await db.insert(decksTable).values(body);
}

// ❌ BAD — raw Drizzle inside a server action
"use server";
export async function createDeck(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  const parsed = createDeckSchema.parse(input);
  await db.insert(decksTable).values({ ...parsed, userId });
}

// ✅ GOOD — server action delegates to a query helper
"use server";
import { insertDeck } from "@/db/queries";

export async function createDeck(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const parsed = createDeckSchema.parse(input);
  await insertDeck({ ...parsed, userId });

  revalidatePath("/dashboard");
}
```

## Validation: Zod Required

All data passed to server actions must be validated with Zod before calling any query helper.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — no validation, using FormData
export async function createDeck(data: FormData) {
  const title = data.get("title");
  await insertDeck({ title, userId });
}

// ✅ GOOD — Zod schema + inferred type
import { z } from "zod";

const createDeckSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  description: z.string().optional(),
});

type CreateDeckInput = z.infer<typeof createDeckSchema>;

export async function createDeck(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const parsed = createDeckSchema.parse(input);
  await insertDeck({ ...parsed, userId });
}
```

- Always use `z.infer<typeof schema>` for the action's parameter type — never write the type manually or use `FormData`.
- Call `.parse()` (throws) or `.safeParse()` (returns result) at the top of every server action before calling any query helper.
- Query helpers own all ownership/scoping logic — callers never repeat `userId` filtering outside of `src/db/queries/`.
